    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`shipping_cost` is implemented in `solution.py` and the 73 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I could not measure line coverage because the only shell command allowed was the test run. Every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by a test, so I expect the 90% gate to pass, but that is unconfirmed. The implementation follows the spec's seven rules: volumetric weight, billable weight rounded up to 0.5 kg, the 8.00 base plus 1.50 per further half kg, the zone factor, free shipping for zones 1–2 at a subtotal of 150 or more, the oversize surcharge (applied after the zone factor and not waived by free shipping), and a single half-up rounding at the end. Where the spec was silent I made two choices: NaN and infinite numbers raise `ValueError`, and `Decimal` is used for all arithmetic so float inputs convert through `str()` as specified. Four of my own test expectations were wrong at first because a 121 cm box with 10 cm sides has a volumetric weight that bills as 2.5 kg; I changed those tests to use 1 cm sides, and the implementation was not touched.",
